//! check: fail(E0301)
//! phase: resolve
//! conforms: gram.expr.tagident, gram.expr.variant
//!
//! wolf-lang#1085: `OPEN` is declared nowhere. A bare capitalized name that
//! names nothing is read as an error tag, and `answer` returns `int`, which
//! has no error row to raise one into, so no row takes it here. That is
//! E0301 at the name (`[gram.expr.tagident]`: a bare identifier no
//! expected row declares misses with E0301), with both fixes named: declare
//! or import the constant, or make `answer` fallible (`-> !int`). Until
//! this row every compiled tier declined it as "an error-row tag outside
//! `!T` context", and lupin 0.1.60 runs it (exit 1, `error: OPEN`).

fn answer() -> int {
    OPEN // ERROR E0301: nothing named `OPEN` is in scope
}

fn main() -> int {
    answer()
}
